## Findings

The new evidence refines the cash-pressure mechanism rather than establishing
a new credit rating. TDG reports approximately 77% fixed-rate gross debt and
approximately 30 USDm additional annual interest cost for a one-percentage-point
rate increase at September 2024. Fixed coupons and derivatives are substantial
counterweights to a generic claim that all debt reprices immediately. However,
swap/cap expiries and forward collar starts alter protection across dates. A
single static hedge percentage cannot represent that schedule.

The downside chain is adverse repricing or input-cost/demand pressure → weaker
cash conversion → less capacity after shareholder distributions and other uses →
greater dependence on accessible cash and facility/refinancing execution. CP-2D
shows positive quarterly OCF alongside a smaller cash balance after financing
outflows. That is actual cash-allocation evidence, not proof of operational
collapse or a failed refinancing. Its December balance is not combined with
the annual rate sensitivity to imply a forward runway.

The arithmetic 91.89 USDm is principal 9,189 times 1%; it is not an independent
net interest forecast. CP-2E's conditional approximately-30 illustration gives
approximately 1,188 annual cash interest, 1,850 OCF-minus-capex proxy and 3.51x
As Defined/cash-interest coverage only under its holding-constant assumptions.
These do not establish true FCF, covenant headroom or effective hedge coverage.
The issuer's historical nonmaterial net-income FX sensitivity likewise cannot
be promoted to zero FX risk or a debt/EBITDA/cash currency map.

Absorbed CP-2F supplies an actual environmental obligation: 5 current plus 36
noncurrent equals 41, versus prior 44. Estimate and payment uncertainty can
consume cash, but the liability is not an incremental stress loss or an immediate
funding demand. Preserve the issuer's contrary expectation that costs beyond
accruals would not materially affect financial position/results on available
information. The appropriate action is to monitor changed estimates, site/payment
plans and third-party contributions. Safety, physical and transition channels
also warrant event-specific monitoring; no realised new event is established.
No ESG score, sustainability debt ratchet or spread/greenium adjustment follows
from the corporate emissions target or missing assurance.

Confidence remains Medium for this bounded historical synthesis; complete macro
sensitivity and forward liquidity sufficiency remain Insufficient Information.
Actual price/cost recovery, continued cash generation, verified protection and
dated accessible liquidity would strengthen the case. Deteriorating conversion,
further extraction or lost protection/access would weaken it.

